        "original_id": "bb2d8cbb-ae50-53d9-be82-a4452515ebf0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Columbia River, Washington, Yakima County, Grant County\n- Organizations: Hanford Site, Grant County Public Utility District\n- Products: Priest Rapids Dam, Wanapum Dam\n- Concepts: hydroelectric dams, nuclear production complexes\n\nFacts:\n- Priest Rapids Dam is a hydroelectric concrete gravity dam on the Columbia River in Washington between the Yakima Firing Range and the Hanford Site, and it spans Yakima County and Grant County.\n- The Hanford Site is a mostly decommissioned nuclear production complex operated by the United States federal government on the Columbia River in Washington.\n- The Hanford Site has also been known as the Hanford Project, Hanford Works, Hanford Engineer Works, and Hanford Nuclear Reservation.\n- Grant County Public Utility District operates the hydroelectric projects Priest Rapids Dam and Wanapum Dam.",
